{
  "id": "COMPOUND:35932 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential pathway where (+)-Caryolan-1-ol interacts with hepatocytes, which in turn are targeted by multiple compounds, including Cocosamide B, (1S,4S,4aR,8aS)-4-[(E)-5-hydroxy-3-methylpent-3-enyl]-4a,8,8-trimethyl-3-methylidene-2,4,5,6,7,8a-hexahydro-1H-naphthalen-1-ol, and 3alpha,4alpha-epoxyrupicoline E. All these compounds are linked to the Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 (MAP3K8) target, indicating a possible role for (+)-Caryolan-1-ol in modulating MAP3K8 activity through its interaction with hepatocytes. The shared target of these compounds suggests a possible mechanism involving hepatocyte signaling pathways, possibly through the MAP3K8 cascade. The evidence is consistent with a role for (+)-Caryolan-1-ol in influencing MAP3K8 activity via hepatocyte-mediated pathways, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
